# HB-SAMPLE (remake phase 2, 2026-10-11): a generated STARTING POINT, not an authored hitbox. Spheres ride the leading limb chain (tip, middle, inner),
# sized from the mesh; timing, damage and reaction are derived from the XV2 hit entry (tools/remake_samples.py, REMAKE-SAMPLES.md). Edit it in the Workbench.
# XV2 hit entry 337; limb foot.R
# DASH TRAVEL (goku-stage 2026-10-11, owner: the dash attack slid too far on friction): retail Falcon's dash attack on Goku's rig (cross_port AttackDash) moves 1.03/frame for 26 frames, then
# 0.27/frame (30.6 units over 41). The row keeps plain flags (dash momentum, not a clip TransN), so the ground speed is re-set every other frame to that x the built size 1.1
# (1.133, then 0.30 world units per frame); friction fills the frames between. About 32 world units over the row's 38 frames.
PUT ANIM_RATE 1.0
wait_until 1
GET ra_f:0 FACING
MUL ra_f:0 1.133
PUT GROUND_VEL ra_f:0
wait_until 3
GET ra_f:0 FACING
MUL ra_f:0 1.133
PUT GROUND_VEL ra_f:0
wait_until 5
GET ra_f:0 FACING
MUL ra_f:0 1.133
PUT GROUND_VEL ra_f:0
hitbox slot=0 joint=@FOOT_R@ damage=12 size=2.8 x=-0.03949 y=-0.4019 z=0.8439 angle=361 kbg=50 fkb=0 bkb=16
hitbox slot=1 joint=@LEG_R@ damage=10 size=5.04 x=0.04702 y=-1.652 z=-0.1287 angle=361 kbg=50 fkb=0 bkb=13
hitbox slot=2 joint=@UPLEG_R@ damage=8 size=5.04 x=-0.1149 y=-1.493 z=-0.08663 angle=361 kbg=50 fkb=0 bkb=10
wait_until 6
